'm a property investor if i was  to offer 80  market value would that be something  that your client would be interested or  open to  so qualify that they're motivated you  cannot be  a motivated buyer you have to be dealing  with motivated sellers  so qualify them and also if you're able  to if you've got cash in your bank  qualify yourself show the estate agent  your proof of deposit  show them your funds show them your  solicitor details  qualify them qualify you it saves a lot  of time and it means that you're going  to be putting yourself in the right  place at the right time  number two is don't speak first when  you're at the viewing  just listen listen to their problems  listen to what their story is listen to  how long they've been trying to sell  why they're trying to sell your job is  to be detective investigator  and find their situation listen don't  speak first and when you speak usually  speak with questions  don't speak first and don't put forward  the offer first  ask them what they'll accept so many  times  i've had situations whereby there's been  a house on the market for a 200 000  pound  i've offered an offer i've put forward  an offer of 180 i thought 20 grand  discount that'd be great  they say yes i'm like  what would have happened if i'd said  160. so don't put forward the offer  first let them speak first  ask them this this is the magic question  you want to say if i was to buy the  property cash tomorrow  what would be the lowest you'd be able  to accept and still live with  that's the question that's the magic  question so write that down did you  notice that was another if would  offer if i was to buy the property cash  tomorrow  what would the lowest you'd be able to  accept with and still live with me like  that's the kind of question you need to  be so don't speak first  listen make them put forward the offer  number three  write this down is expect to be rejected  if you want to be successful in property  if you want to find some  